{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115799","id":3239283731,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7BE4wT","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115799","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115799.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115799.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115799","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115799/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115799/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115799/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f3a815238b5e7c12f421a6f63c0d94830dfabd96","number":115799,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add view count support to Viewport","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds the ability to configure the view count (layers) on a Viewport. Before this was only possible inside of the renderer itself through an overrule when `use_xr` is on.\r\n\r\nThis allows us to create additional viewports that use the layer system and no longer be restricted to the primary XR output. This enabled:\r\n- Creating an additional stereo viewport for foveated inset rendering.\r\n- Creating an additional stereo viewport for mirror effects.\r\n- Creating an additional stereo viewport to  use as a composition layer (render hands and pointers separately so they render above UI composition layers).\r\nFor some of the above we also need camera changes but those our outside of the scope of this PR. \r\n\r\nIt also moves the XR viewport size overrule out of the render server and into the Viewport class. This is currently a \"polling\" approach just like it was in the rendering server, the logic is already smart enough not to rebuild the viewport if the size has not changed.\r\n\r\nThis also has the bonus effect that accurate size information will be available on the Viewport node when XR is used. A limitation of the old approach that caused issues in the past. \r\n\r\nTriggering output to the HMD and other overrules such as destination buffer overrides and dynamic resolution changes remain internal to the rendering engine and triggered by the `use_xr` flag. Some of these we may address at some point in the future but marking a Viewport as the primary XR output will remain.\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> This extracts some core improvements from other PRs that attempted quad view/inset rendering so they can be reviewed in isolation. We're looking into an improved implementation to foveated inset rendering that will rely on this logic.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id